hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer a question  from one of my newsletter readers  Christine who's an entrepreneur  and she's a tour operator so she takes  tourists around in Kenya who are  visiting and shows him a good time which  was in the country pretty new business  and one of my advice on growing it so  she has three main target markets that  she's going after one are the tourists  so international tourists looking to  view the country the second are  honeymooners so people coming just after  getting married and on vacation and the  third are corporate clients and they're  often coming for different team-building  activities so Christine having been on a  number of trips myself internationally  and I've never been to Africa but I've  gone to a number of different countries  on trips especially when you're coming  off of cruise ships or you're looking  for two offers to go with the biggest  thing that I think you can offer is  service most of the time when you land  I don't think especially offer cruise  ships when you let you get off and  there's a thousand different tour  operators coming at you and you don't  know how to differentiate one for the  other and the biggest fear that you're  going to have is that you're going to  make a mistake and go with the wrong  person you're gonna have a bad  experience some people worried about  safety depending on the country they're  going into but for most part is having a  bad experience and being stuck for a  whole day with the tour operator who's  not going to give you either good value  or good service and it's really really  hard to tell what a good service is  going to be for bad service just from  landing on you know going to the dock or  going to the airport and seeing the  people kind of pitching you the  different ideas so it's the biggest fear  that people going to have and for agents  who are going to be referring you for  international travel agents who are  booking trips on behalf of these guys  it's also really hard for them to tell  who's going to provide good service or  not so service five-star service  excellent service is really going to  help you stand out so it's a couple  different ways you can do it the first  thing I would do is I would put people  in uniforms  if you have somebody in uniform and I  appreciate that it's very hot in Kenya  so you know short sleeves shorts even  but something that looks professional if  you did that right away you're going to  stand out from everybody else is on  coming at you so I've been to a lot of  different cities and countries and again  you're pitched by all sorts of people  and they often look you know they're in  regular street clothes you don't really  know this is a company or just some guy  in the back of his van that you're  getting into so if you had professional  sign professional uniforms that people  were into you're already setting a  standard of service that's higher than  everybody else and it's going to be a  lot easier for you to get the  north-american clients who are looking  for some kind of trust and people put a  lot of trust in that service and having  uniforms the next thing make sure  everything is clean and make sure  everybody you hire is super friendly so  clean again if they're in uniform make  sure the uniforms are clean whatever  vehicle they're coming to pick people up  in make sure those are clean because a  lot of times they're not in a lot of  countries that I've been to at least  make sure the signage is clean it's not  all scuffed up and people handing you  kind of photocopies of things that don't  look very professional you want to have  a professional image and you can even  charge a premium people who are on  vacation or who are honeymooning or  corporate they are looking to spend  money right when I get off on a cruise  ship and I'm landing in a country I want  to spend money I want to have a good  time I'm just worried I'm going to spend  it with the wrong person so people would  pay you a premium to ensure that they're  going to have a really good experience  and that's why people on cruise ships  often booked through the cruise operator  because they know they're going to get a  pretty good experience and it's been  vetted by the cruise ship before but  it's a huge huge price increase and  they're willing to pay it so if you can  immediately off the off the boat or  people line it on their plane or however  they're getting there show them that you  look highly professional and guarantee  they're going to have a good experience  you're going to be able to charge your  premium and get more business so again  everything must be clean and you want  people to be friendly so greet with a  smile ask people how they're doing you  know you want to Train anybody who is  working on the front lines dealing with  customers to be friendly answer  questions make it a good time people are  there to have fun so you want to make  sure you're having fun people who your  hire is  something that I would also encourage  you to do and I don't know how feasible  it is but I would try to hire expats or  students from the countries that you're  trying to recruit from so for example if  you're trying to attract Americans to  come in and sign up I would try to get  an expat American or American students  to be there selling your services for  you if I see somebody who is more like  me you're more likely to sign up with  them and a quick example when I went to  Japan I was the only guy from from North  American work at sea in Japan there's  you know very Japanese centric which is  great and and immediately you're faced  with culture shock so you're not quite  sure what to do you may not understand  the language you're walking around  you're not quite sure where you're going  and there was another guy who I met on  the streets who was from North America  and immediately you make friends because  you're the only two who are the same and  everybody else is is different vistas  big culture shock and immediately we  were able to strike up conversation  start talking he introduced me to you  know where he was hanging out and gave  me gave me some recommendations so I can  see the same thing happening where it  could be a big culture shock for  somebody from North America coming to  Kenya not knowing you know where to go  not knowing the language the culture so  if you had somebody working for your  company who was from North America or UK  or Australia who spoke the language once  the culture and could speak with people  on their own terms in their own in their  own culture it'd be a lot easier to get  people to sign up so if a tour operator  came to me in any of the countries that  I landed in and it was somebody from the  US or Canada or or Britain I'd be a lot  more willing to start talking to them  and be easier for me to sign up with  them if they were clean-cut friendly in  uniform and look like me it'd be a lot  easier for me to want to do business  with them so just because there's so  much culture shock it's an easy way for  you to stand out now you still want to  provide the Kenyan experience where  people are there to experience Kenya but  if you had some people in the front  lines who are more like the people who  you're selling to as much as you can  relate to your customer the easier it is  to be able to sell them  look at if there's any expats or  students from the countries to be able  to bring them on board to be on your  front lines as well to help talk to  customers the last thing we do then is  also get on TripAdvisor and encourage  people to leave positive comments so  whenever we do any of our travels will  always go on TripAdvisor and see what  are the most common things that people  do where it's getting the most feedback  and we're trying to plan our day right  we may not have a lot of time in  whatever city we're going to whatever  country so we want to make sure it's  time well-spent and you're getting kind  of the maximum value from it so to  provide is a great place to go and if we  see that one to operator is getting tons  of great remarks for the great service  they have and how friendly everybody is  and how clean everybody is I'm gonna go  and book with those guys even if it's at  a premium to everybody else and I'll  probably even do the booking in advance  to make sure I get my spot so then  there's less sales that you'll have to  do when people get there they're already  pre booking and that'll help with a lot  of your cash flow issues as well because  people are paying upfront and you're  delivering the service whenever they  arrive in in your country so hopefully  that helps might be a little different  than what you're expecting but I think  there's a real opportunity for you to be  able to stand out using that five-star  service methodology and be able to get a  lot of those people to come and want to  work with you and pay you more money  than they'd be paying the other guys so  hopefully that helps if you guys liked  the video please give it a thumbs up  below and I also look forward to hearing  your comments if you want to leave one  under the video and stay tuned for next  episode  you  you
 

